  "scene": {
    "id": "overlap-pilot4",
    "language": "All right, so how overlapping works is I'm in a situation right now, or you're in a situation where you have the ball and the opponent is in front of you. I'm behind you. You want to try to score, but you can't because right now the opponent is right in front of you defending. So what you're gonna do instead is I'm gonna overlap you to get to a better position, and then you could then pass the ball to me, where then I can then make the choice if I want to take it to the goal or pass it back to you. So let's see how this works. [0][1][2][3]Okay, now I have the ball and now I could either choose to pass it to you or take it straight to the goal. In this situation, since the opponent is kind of between us and I have a reasonable distance and they're not in my clear path to the goal, I have a pass to the goal so that I can directly ch- shoot it straight to the goal.[4][5][6]",
